# tools/cp/hunt/reload2.p9 -- the P9 reload without the H1-12 trap (lane
# H1-hunt round 2, docs/cp-hunt.md).  tools/cp/p9/reload.p9 first opens the
# save list (evidence) and Esc's back; after that Esc the main menu shows no
# focus frame for Up/Down (cp-hunt H1-12, 3/3 boots), so its CONTINUE seek
# fails.  Here CONTINUE (= the newest save, boot A's quick save) is taken from
# the FRESH main menu, where the focus behaves (every boot so far).  The save
# list is not shown; the evidence that the save is boot A's is the world
# itself: an immediate F5 without moving writes a new quick save whose
# metadata playerPosition tools/cp/p9/saves.sh compares with boot A's.
phase menu
shot menu
expect menu-continue 10 CONTINUE
# No `seek` here: in h2-rl2 the reading after the 2nd Up was one 104 px
# frame over CONTINUE + NEW GAME (the CONTINUE highlight drawn taller, or
# caught moving), labelled NEW GAME by its centre, so seek tapped once more and
# overshot onto the frameless button above CONTINUE.  Every fresh main menu so
# far (h2-rl1, h2-rl2, round 1's reloads) answered the 1st Up with NEW GAME and
# the 2nd with CONTINUE, so: two Ups with a settle gap, a shot for the record,
# and the `expect loaded` below is the check (Enter on anything but CONTINUE
# does not reach the loading screen's PRESS ... TO CONTINUE).
key up
wait 1.6
shot menu-continue-a
key up
wait 1.6
shot menu-continue-b
phase loading
key ret
expect loaded 400 PRESS\b.{0,24}\bTO\s+CONTINUE
key spc
wait 6
phase world
expect inworld 60 RIPPERDOC|Jackie
shot reloaded-place
wait 10
shot reloaded-place2
# quick save WITHOUT moving: its playerPosition must equal boot A's last save
phase save
key f5
wait 5
shot resaved
# ~2 minutes in the world (an fps sample on the reloaded save)
phase world
repeat 5
hold w 4000
look 400 0 20 16
down shift
hold w 4000
up shift
wait 3
shot rl-loop
end
phase quit
key esc
wait 4
seek pause-quit pause down 9 QUIT GAME
exit_ok
key ret
wait 3
expect quit-confirm 10 sure.{0,20}quit
key ret
wait_exit 180
